    "R2-3_signed_deviation_ablation": {
      "sentence": "Contrary to the premise this check was originally scoped around, removing Signed_Deviation substantially HURTS recovery: held-out ARI drops from 0.851 to 0.451 (K-Means) and 0.472 to 0.242 (HMM); Right Bias recall collapses from 1.000 to exactly 0.000 (Left Bias: 1.000 to 0.779). Mechanism (verified directly, not inferred): Signed_Deviation is the only feature carrying LEFT-vs-RIGHT direction -- Choice_Deviation is its absolute value, so it flags that bias exists but not which side. Without the signed feature, 633/806 true Right Bias trials are assigned to the Left Bias cluster (both directions merge), and the cluster Hungarian-matched to the 'Right Bias' label is actually {'Engaged': 1216, 'Exploration': 1028, 'Left Bias': 1, 'Right Bias': 0} by true label -- a non-bias cluster, not a genuine Right Bias recovery.",
